# CODEOWNERS for Zharp.
#
# GitHub reads this file to decide who gets automatically requested for review on a
# pull request. Later matching rules win over earlier ones, so the catch-all comes
# first and the per directory rules below it are the ones that actually apply.
#
# Note that this file only requests reviews. It does not block anything on its own:
# review is only enforced once a branch protection rule on `main` turns on
# "Require review from Code Owners".

# Everything in the repo, unless a rule below overrides it.
*                   @LupuC

# Windows app, C# and WinUI 3.
/windows/           @LupuC

# macOS app, Swift and AppKit.
/macos/             @LupuC

# Linux port. No code yet, the toolkit has not been chosen. See linux/README.md.
/linux/             @LupuC

# Platform neutral assets shared by every app: icons, fonts, brand files, and
# anything else all three platforms compile or ship.
#
# This directory deliberately requires maintainer review. A change here is never
# local: swapping a font, renaming an icon, or editing a shared colour ripples into
# the Windows build, the macOS build, and eventually the Linux one, and a mistake
# breaks all of them at once. Review here is about that blast radius, not distrust.
/shared/            @LupuC
